	<section class="main-content">
		<div class="container">

			<div class="container-sm">
				
									<div class="main-content__text">
						<p><b><i>‘You know Goblin, when you first started appearing to me, I thought you were a figment of my imagination… I&#8217;m not alone at all. I have you Goblin.’</i></b></p>
<p>2007. Decatur, Illinois (aka America’s asscrack). With a cursed family at home and the class bully set on outing him to the entire school, life for 15-year-old emo kid Eliot is far from easy.</p>
<p>But through it all he has us. His confidants. His goblins.</p>
<p>That is until he meets the much older reality TV star Max, and they begin a destructive relationship that will change everything.</p>
<p>Written &amp; performed by<strong> Derek Mitchell</strong> (known online as @derekscottmitchell and @letsdoubledutch), <em><strong>Goblin</strong></em> is a “seriously impressive” (The Stage) dark, comedic solo performance about obsession, growing up and the transformative power of being seen.</p>
<p>Told through vivid characters, shifting voices and physical transformation, this pitch-black comedy asks, can a man who has lost himself find his goblin again?</p>
<p><em>Daddy&#8217;s Money Productions in association with Park Theatre </em></p>
<p><span data-ccp-props="{}"> </span></p>

					</div>
							</div>

											
